.TH VIPER4LINUX 1 "November 2026" "ViPER4Linux-RE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
viper4linux \- start or reuse the native ViPER4Linux-RE backend and Qt6 GUI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B viper4linux
.RI [ --help | --fingerprint | --preflight | --restart-backend ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B viper4linux
command is a symbolic link to the same native executable as
.BR v4l-cli .
With no arguments, it starts or reuses the matching marked ViPER PipeWire
filter-chain backend and Audio Output monitor, then opens the Qt6 GUI.
A second launch activates the existing GUI instead of creating a duplicate.
Backend fingerprints include the built DSP, controller binary and routing
configuration. A mismatched marked backend may be replaced, but unrelated
PipeWire clients and the system PipeWire service are never stopped.
.PP
The shorter
.B v4l-cli
command provides effect controls and explicit lifecycle operations.
The Python Audio Output monitor remains an independent worker, but the
former Python application launcher has been retired.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show launcher usage without starting anything.
.TP
.B --fingerprint
Print a SHA-256 fingerprint of the DSP, controller and PipeWire routing
configuration. Does not start, restart or stop any process.
.TP
.B --preflight
Inspect the backend and report whether a normal launch would start,
reuse or replace its marked client. Read-only snapshot, not a lock.
.TP
.B --restart-backend
Restart the marked ViPER backend and Audio Output monitor without starting
another GUI. Wait for a fresh monitor heartbeat before reporting success.
.SH CLI LIFECYCLE COMMANDS
Run these via
.BR v4l-cli :
.TP
.B --quit-gui
Quit the GUI and keep the ViPER backend processing audio. Does not change
remembered GUI quit preferences.
.TP
.B --quit-all
Quit the GUI and stop the marked ViPER backend. If the GUI is absent, stop
only the marked backend; never signal system PipeWire.
.TP
.B --restart-backend
Restart the ViPER backend and its Audio Output monitor. The GUI stays open,
and current settings are restored by the backend's normal persistence path.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ViPERforLinux/ViPERClean.conf
Current effect settings and GUI preferences.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/viper4linux/presets/
Saved named effect presets.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/viper4linux/backend.log
Combined timestamped backend/monitor diagnostics.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR viper4linux-ctl (1),
.BR v4l-cli (1)
